{title: Rise up and help us}
{subtitle: Psalms 44:26–27}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]For your sake we [Bb]are killed all [Dm]day
Regarded as [Bb]sheep for the slaughter
[Dm]Awake Lord why [Bb]do you sleep
[Dm]Rouse yourself do not [Bb]reject us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Rise [Bb]up and help [C]us
Re[Dm]deem us [Bb]for your [C]steadfast love
[Dm]Rise [Bb]up and help [C]us
Our soul [Bb]is sunk [C]down to the [Dm]dust [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Why do you [Bb]hide your [Dm]face
Forget our [Bb]affliction and op[Dm]pression
Our bo[Bb]dy clings to the ground [Dm]
We wait for [Bb]your faithful hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Rise [Bb]up and help [C]us
Re[Dm]deem us [Bb]for your [C]steadfast love
[Dm]Rise [Bb]up and help [C]us
Our soul [Bb]is sunk [C]down to the [Dm]dust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]We are regard[C]ed as sheep
[Dm]Waiting for the dawn to break
[Bb]Do not for[C]get our cries
Remem[Bb]ber our suf[C]fering pain
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Rise [Bb]up and help [C]us
Re[Dm]deem us for [Bb]your stead[C]fast love
{end_of_verse}
